{"id":"9e153f9db0baf9683a09bffead5e58464ae43bbd","axis":"silent","repo":"rustwasm/wasm-bindgen","sha":"9e153f9db0baf9683a09bffead5e58464ae43bbd","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -8,8 +8,22 @@"," * Added `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` release artifacts.","   [#5439](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5439)"," ","+* `catch` on an import returning `js_sys::Promise<T>` rather than a `Result`","+  returns a synchronous throw as a rejected promise, so the error surfaces at","+  `.await` instead of unwinding through Wasm. The conversion goes through the","+  new `wasm_bindgen::convert::FromCaughtException` trait, which js-sys","+  implements for `Promise<T, E>`.","+  [#5442](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5442)","+"," ### Changed"," ","+* Awaiting a `js_sys::Promise<T, E>` converts the rejection reason through","+  `E: From<JsValue>` rather than `E: FromWasmAbi`, as a `catch` import's","+  error does, since JS can reject with any value. JS types still convert","+  unchecked, a Rust error type can inspect the reason, and a value type such","+  as `String` is no longer accepted as `E` there.","+  [#5442](https://github.com/wasm-bindgen/wasm-bindgen/pull/5442)","+"," ### Fixed"," "," ### Removed"],"additions":14,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/js-sys/src/futures/mod.rs","lines":["@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ struct Inner<T = JsValue, E = JsValue> {","     task: Option<Waker>,","     callbacks: Option<(","         Closure<dyn FnMut(T) -> Result<(), JsError>>,","-        Closure<dyn FnMut(E) -> Result<(), JsError>>,","+        Closure<dyn FnMut(JsValue) -> Result<(), JsError>>,","     )>,"," }"," ","@@ -154,9 +154,9 @@ struct Inner<T = JsValue, E = JsValue> {"," /// with the JavaScript `Promise`."," ///"," /// A `JsFuture<T, E>` built from a `Promise<T, E>` resolves to","-/// `Result<T, E>`: the fulfilled value is converted as a `T` and the","-/// rejection reason as an `E`, both unchecked, just as JS could have","-/// settled the promise with anything.","+/// `Result<T, E>`. The fulfilled value is converted as a `T`, unchecked, as","+/// any declared return is. The rejection reason is whatever JS threw, so it","+/// converts through `E: From<JsValue>`, as a `catch` import's error does."," ///"," /// Currently this type is constructed with `JsFuture::from`."," pub struct JsFuture<T = JsValue, E = JsValue> {","@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@ impl<T, E> fmt::Debug for JsFuture<T, E> {"," // no layout equivalence with `JsValue` is required at this seam — the"," // per-type `from_abi` does the conversion (e.g. for dynamic unions it"," // runs the variant dispatcher).","-impl<T: FromWasmAbi + 'static, E: FromWasmAbi + 'static> From<Promise<T, E>> for JsFuture<T, E> {","+impl<T: FromWasmAbi + 'static, E: From<JsValue> + 'static> From<Promise<T, E>> for JsFuture<T, E> {","     fn from(js: Promise<T, E>) -> JsFuture<T, E> {","         // Use the `then` method to schedule two callbacks, one for the","         // resolved value and one for the rejected value. We're currently","@@ -248,12 +248,13 @@ impl<T: FromWasmAbi + 'static, E: FromWasmAbi + 'static> From<Promise<T, E>> for"," ","         let reject = {","             let state = AssertUnwindSafe(state.clone());","-            Closure::once(move |val: E| {","-                finish(&*state, Err(val));","+            Closure::once(move |val: JsValue| {","+                finish(&*state, Err(E::from(val)));","                 Ok(())","             })","         };"," ","+        let js: Promise<T> = js.unchecked_into();","         let _ = js.then_with_reject(&resolve, &reject);"," ","         state.borrow_mut().callbacks = Some((resolve, reject));","@@ -280,7 +281,7 @@ impl<T, E> Future for JsFuture<T, E> {","     }"," }"," ","-impl<T: FromWasmAbi + 'static, E: FromWasmAbi + 'static> IntoFuture for Promise<T, E> {","+impl<T: FromWasmAbi + 'static, E: From<JsValue> + 'static> IntoFuture for Promise<T, E> {","     type Output = Result<T, E>;","     type IntoFuture = JsFuture<T, E>;"," "],"additions":9,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/js-sys/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -14590,6 +14590,14 @@ impl<T, E> Promising for Promise<T, E> {","     type Resolution = T;"," }"," ","+/// A `catch` import returning `Promise<T, E>` returns a synchronous throw as","+/// a rejected promise.","+impl<T, E> wasm_bindgen::convert::FromCaughtException for Promise<T, E> {","+    fn from_caught_exception(e: JsValue) -> Self {","+        Promise::<T>::reject_typed(&e).unchecked_into()","+    }","+}","+"," /// Internal: maps a tuple of `Promise<T_i, E>` to the result shapes of"," /// [`Promise::all_tuple`] and [`Promise::all_settled_tuple`]."," ///"],"additions":8,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/js-sys/tests/wasm/Promise.js","lines":["@@ -108,3 +108,21 @@ export async function stringOrTypeError(value, fail) {"," export function rejectTypeError(message) {","   return Promise.reject(new TypeError(message));"," }","+","+export function maybeAsync(fail) {","+  if (fail) throw new Error('sync');","+  return Promise.resolve('ok');","+}","+","+export class Thrower {","+  static maybeAsync(fail) {","+    return maybeAsync(fail);","+  }","+  maybeAsync(fail) {","+    return maybeAsync(fail);","+  }","+  echo(value, fail) {","+    if (fail) throw new Error('sync');","+    return Promise.resolve(value);","+  }","+}"],"additions":18,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/js-sys/tests/wasm/Promise.rs","lines":["@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@"," use js_sys::*;","+use wasm_bindgen::convert::{FromWasmAbi, RefIntoWasmAbi};"," use wasm_bindgen::prelude::*;"," use wasm_bindgen::{JsCast, JsError};"," use wasm_bindgen_futures::{future_to_promise_typed, JsFuture};","@@ -826,3 +827,62 @@ async fn typed_rejection_combinators() {","     let err: JsValue = Promise::race_iterable(&arr).await.unwrap_err();","     assert!(err.is_instance_of::<TypeError>());"," }","+","+#[wasm_bindgen(module = \"tests/wasm/Promise.js\")]","+extern \"C\" {","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch, js_name = maybeAsync)]","+    fn maybe_async(fail: bool) -> Promise<String>;","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch, experimental_generic_mono, js_name = maybeAsync)]","+    fn maybe_async_like(fail: impl JsBooleanOrStringLike) -> Promise<String>;","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch, js_name = maybeAsync)]","+    fn maybe_async_message(fail: bool) -> Promise<String, Message>;","+","+    type Thrower;","+    #[wasm_bindgen(constructor)]","+    fn new() -> Thrower;","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch, method, js_name = maybeAsync)]","+    fn run(this: &Thrower, fail: bool) -> Promise<String>;","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch, static_method_of = Thrower, js_name = maybeAsync)]","+    fn make(fail: bool) -> Promise<String>;","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch, method, experimental_generic_mono, js_name = echo)]","+    fn echo<T: RefIntoWasmAbi>(this: &Thrower, value: &T, fail: bool) -> Promise<T>;","+}","+","+#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]","+struct Message(String);","+","+impl From<JsValue> for Message {","+    fn from(value: JsValue) -> Self {","+        Message(value.unchecked_into::<Error>().message().into())","+    }","+}","+","+// A sync throw and an async rejection both reach `E` through `From<JsValue>`.","+#[wasm_bindgen_test]","+async fn catch_rejects_sync_throws_as_typed_error() {","+    assert_eq!(maybe_async_message(false).await.unwrap(), \"ok\");","+    assert_eq!(","+        maybe_async_message(true).await.unwrap_err(),","+        Message(\"sync\".into())","+    );","+    let rejected: Promise<String, Message> =","+        Promise::<String>::reject_typed(&Error::new(\"async\").into()).unchecked_into();","+    assert_eq!(rejected.await.unwrap_err(), Message(\"async\".into()));","+}","+","+#[wasm_bindgen_test]","+async fn catch_rejects_sync_throws() {","+    async fn message<T: FromWasmAbi + 'static>(p: Promise<T>) -> String {","+        String::from(p.await.err().unwrap().unchecked_into::<Error>().message())","+    }","+    assert_eq!(maybe_async(false).await.unwrap(), \"ok\");","+    assert_eq!(message(maybe_async(true)).await, \"sync\");","+    assert_eq!(maybe_async_like(\"\").await.unwrap(), \"ok\");","+    assert_eq!(message(maybe_async_like(\"fail\")).await, \"sync\");","+    let t = Thrower::new();","+    assert_eq!(t.run(false).await.unwrap(), \"ok\");","+    assert_eq!(message(t.run(true)).await, \"sync\");","+    assert_eq!(message(Thrower::make(true)).await, \"sync\");","+    assert_eq!(t.echo(&2.5, false).await.unwrap(), 2.5);","+    assert_eq!(message(t.echo(&\"x\".to_string(), true)).await, \"sync\");","+}"],"additions":60,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/js-sys/tests/wasm/futures.rs","lines":["@@ -372,6 +372,32 @@ async fn typed_promise_await_reject() {","     assert_eq!(e.message(), \"t\");"," }"," ","+// A rejection converts through `From<JsValue>`, so a Rust error type can","+// inspect the arbitrary value JS rejected with.","+#[derive(Debug, PartialEq)]","+struct Rejected(String);","+","+impl From<JsValue> for Rejected {","+    fn from(value: JsValue) -> Self {","+        use wasm_bindgen::JsCast;","+        match value.dyn_into::<js_sys::Error>() {","+            Ok(e) => Rejected(e.message().into()),","+            Err(other) => Rejected(format!(\"{other:?}\")),","+        }","+    }","+}","+","+#[wasm_bindgen_test]","+async fn typed_promise_await_reject_from_js_value() {","+    use js_sys::{Number, TypeError};","+    use wasm_bindgen::JsCast;","+    let p: Promise<Number, Rejected> =","+        Promise::<JsValue>::reject(&TypeError::new(\"t\").into()).unchecked_into();","+    assert_eq!(p.await.unwrap_err(), Rejected(\"t\".into()));","+    let p: Promise<Number, Rejected> = Promise::<JsValue>::reject(&5.into()).unchecked_into();","+    assert_eq!(p.await.unwrap_err(), Rejected(\"JsValue(5)\".into()));","+}","+"," // A typed `JsFuture` is `UnwindSafe`, as `future_to_promise` requires under"," // panic=unwind."," #[allow(dead_code)]"],"additions":26,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/macro-support/src/ast.rs","lines":["@@ -207,6 +207,9 @@ pub struct ImportFunction {","     pub js_ret: Option<syn::Type>,","     /// Whether to catch JS exceptions","     pub catch: bool,","+    /// `catch` on a `Promise<..>` return: a synchronous throw is returned","+    /// through `FromCaughtException` as a rejected promise.","+    pub catch_rejects: bool,","     /// Whether the function is variadic on the JS side","     pub variadic: bool,","     /// Whether the function should use structural type checking"],"additions":3,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/macro-support/src/codegen.rs","lines":["@@ -3187,7 +3187,15 @@ impl ast::ImportFunction {","         }"," ","         let mut exceptional_ret = quote!();","-        if self.catch && !self.function.r#async && !self.suspending {","+        if self.catch_rejects {","+            if self.function.r#async || self.suspending {","+                bail_span!(","+                    self.rust_name,","+                    \"`catch` on an `async` or `suspending` import needs a `Result` return\"","+                );","+            }","+            exceptional_ret = catch_rejects_ret(wasm_bindgen, &self.function);","+        } else if self.catch && !self.function.r#async && !self.suspending {","             convert_ret = quote! { Ok(#convert_ret) };","             exceptional_ret = quote! {","                 #wasm_bindgen::__rt::take_last_exception()?;","@@ -4088,7 +4096,15 @@ impl ast::ImportFunction {","         }"," ","         let mut exceptional_ret = quote!();","-        if self.catch && !self.function.r#async {","+        if self.catch_rejects {","+            if self.function.r#async {","+                bail_span!(","+                    self.rust_name,","+                    \"`catch` on an `async` import needs a `Result` return\"","+                );","+            }","+            exceptional_ret = catch_rejects_ret(wasm_bindgen, &self.function);","+        } else if self.catch && !self.function.r#async {","             convert_ret = quote! { Ok(#convert_ret) };","             exceptional_ret = quote! {","                 #wasm_bindgen::__rt::take_last_exception()?;","@@ -6186,6 +6202,17 @@ fn fn_trait_bound_sig(","     None"," }"," ","+/// A `catch` import returning `Promise<..>` hands a synchronous throw to its","+/// return type, before the (then meaningless) return value is converted.","+fn catch_rejects_ret(wasm_bindgen: &syn::Path, function: &ast::Function) -> TokenStream {","+    let ret = &function.ret.as_ref().unwrap().r#type;","+    quote! {","+        if let Err(e) = #wasm_bindgen::__rt::take_last_exception() {","+            return <#ret as #wasm_bindgen::convert::FromCaughtException>::from_caught_exception(e);","+        }","+    }","+}","+"," #[cfg(test)]"," mod tests {","     use super::*;"],"additions":29,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/macro-support/src/parser.rs","lines":["@@ -1019,7 +1019,12 @@ impl<'a>","         )?;","         let catch = opts.catch().is_some();","         let variadic = opts.variadic().is_some();","-        let js_ret = if catch {","+        let catch_rejects = catch","+            && wasm","+                .ret","+                .as_ref()","+                .is_some_and(|ret| last_segment_is(&ret.r#type, \"Promise\"));","+        let js_ret = if catch && !catch_rejects {","             // TODO: this assumes a whole bunch:","             //","             // * The outer type is actually a `Result`","@@ -1327,6 +1332,7 @@ impl<'a>","             kind,","             js_ret,","             catch,","+            catch_rejects,","             variadic,","             structural: opts.structural().is_some() || opts.r#final().is_none(),","             rust_name: self.sig.ident,","@@ -3860,6 +3866,15 @@ fn main(program: &ast::Program, mut f: ItemFn, tokens: &mut TokenStream) -> Resu","     Ok(())"," }"," ","+fn last_segment_is(ty: &syn::Type, name: &str) -> bool {","+    match get_ty(ty) {","+        syn::Type::Path(syn::TypePath {","+            qself: None, path, ..","+        }) => path.segments.last().is_some_and(|seg| seg.ident == name),","+        _ => false,","+    }","+}","+"," #[cfg(test)]"," mod tests {","     #[test]"],"additions":16,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"guide/src/reference/attributes/on-js-imports/catch.md","lines":["@@ -22,6 +22,25 @@ If calling the imported function throws an exception, then `Err` will be"," returned with the exception that was raised. Otherwise, `Ok` is returned with"," the result of the function."," ","+An import returning a `js_sys::Promise<T>` may instead keep its `Promise`","+return. A synchronous throw is then returned as a rejected promise, so it","+surfaces where the promise is awaited, as it would for an `async` JS function:","+","+```rust","+#[wasm_bindgen]","+extern \"C\" {","+    #[wasm_bindgen(catch)]","+    fn fetch_text(url: &str) -> Promise<String>;","+}","+","+// `Err` here whether `fetchText` threw or its promise rejected.","+let result = fetch_text(\"/\").await;","+```","+","+The return type converts the exception through the","+`wasm_bindgen::convert::FromCaughtException` trait, which `js-sys` implements","+for `Promise<T, E>`.","+"," > By default `wasm-bindgen` will take no action when Wasm calls a JS function"," > which ends up throwing an exception. The Wasm spec right now doesn't support"," > stack unwinding and as a result Rust code **will not execute destructors**."],"additions":19,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"guide/src/reference/js-promises-and-rust-futures.md","lines":["@@ -52,9 +52,10 @@ async fn load_config() -> Result<Object, TypeError> {"," }"," ```"," ","-Like `T`, `E` is an unchecked assertion about the JS side: JS can reject","-with any value, and the rejection reason is converted as an `E` without a","-check. Both parameters are covariant, so a `Promise<T, TypeError>` upcasts","+JS can reject with any value, so the rejection reason converts through","+`E: From<JsValue>`, as a `catch` import's error does. For a JS type such as","+`TypeError` that is an unchecked cast, while a Rust error type can implement","+`From<JsValue>` to inspect the reason. Both parameters are covariant, so a `Promise<T, TypeError>` upcasts"," to `Promise<T, Error>` or to `Promise<T>`, and a `JsFuture<T, E>` does the"," same."," "],"additions":4,"deletions":3,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/convert/traits.rs","lines":["@@ -913,3 +913,10 @@ impl_js_string_like!(","     &alloc::boxed::Box<str>,","     &alloc::borrow::Cow<'_, str>,"," );","+","+/// The return type of a `catch` import that isn't a `Result`: a synchronous","+/// JS throw is returned as `from_caught_exception(e)`. js-sys implements it","+/// for `Promise<T>` as a rejected promise, so the throw arrives at `.await`.","+pub trait FromCaughtException {","+    fn from_caught_exception(e: JsValue) -> Self;","+}",""],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":213,"deletions":14,"truncated":false,"file_count":12},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-05T16:29:43.281807+00:00"}